//// css — the base for building CSS (decision 338): a reader of a stylesheet
//// into a typed `Sheet`, its renderer, and `scope(id, css)`.
////
//// Pure `.bp` only: no host cell, no `declare fn`, no sidecar; it imports
//// `std` and nothing else, and it compiles for erlang and commonJS. It knows
//// no framework and no file kind: the scope id is a string its caller hands
//// it. Consumers write `import {sheet.scope, sheet.parse} from "css";`.
////
//// Modules are listed so a module precedes the siblings that import it.

pub mod chars;
pub mod selector;
pub mod sheet;
